{"connection_id": "BC-f519338b1c566f8c3482", "ref": "1 Clement 37:5", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "small and great bodily members together", "note": "The source compares mutual counsel to parts joined in a body; Clement's discussion of members says the body requires both small and great parts to function together, extending the anatomical image to church order."}
{"connection_id": "BC-bb4dc9fdc2491cf8e7c5", "ref": "1 Clement 38:1", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "strong provide for weak", "note": "The commentary's good deeds attach people and repair what is weak; Clement asks strong members to care for weak members and rich ones to supply the poor, giving the jointed body a practical obligation."}
{"connection_id": "BC-98253a89e2566e627723", "ref": "Ignatius, Ephesians 9:1", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "believers as stones of Father's temple", "note": "The commentary builds a sound structure from its believers' deeds; Ignatius pictures his addressees as stones of the Father's temple raised by the cross, with faith and love involved in their movement."}
{"connection_id": "BC-349e549c698204c42f1b", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.12.25", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "members care for one another without division", "note": "The commentary makes counsel connect parts; Paul says the body should have no division and its members should have the same care for one another, giving bodily cohesion a reciprocal ethical consequence."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b50b47f34e0c5f28d38c", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.12.25", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "no division; members care for each other", "note": "The commentary's joined parts are also people who counsel one another; Paul says bodily members should have no division but equal care for each other."}
{"connection_id": "BC-160865cd269d48c792f7", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.14.26", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "speech in assembly for building up", "note": "The commentary calls firmly formed words part of a common building; Paul requires each contribution to the gathering to be for building up the community."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7f9b2de0b76d75e558dd", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.15.58", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "steadfast labor not in vain", "note": "The commentary opposes durable, beneficial work to loss; Paul calls believers steadfast and abundant in the Lord's work because their labor is not vain, joining firmness, work, and gain."}
{"connection_id": "BC-aa068da7a567f6cd79f5", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.3.10", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "builder lays a foundation and must take care how he builds", "note": "The commentary makes construction an image for coordinated action; Paul describes himself as a skilled builder who laid a foundation and warns each builder to take care, making workmanship and responsibility explicit."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a4ff356cd6a332a4e83d", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.3.10", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "skilled builder and how each builds", "note": "The commentary's builder places bricks as deeds; Paul calls himself a skilled foundation-layer and warns each subsequent builder to consider how he builds on it."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8a4fa5559863f239076f", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.3.11", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "foundation that cannot be replaced", "note": "The source compares secure and collapsing foundations; Paul says no one can lay a foundation other than Jesus Christ, specifying why the community's building can be sound."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ffc726e951ac5cfd4ed5", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.3.12", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "gold, stone, wood, hay, straw as building materials", "note": "The commentary distinguishes sound construction from the spider’s weak house; Paul lists materials of sharply different durability for what people build, making the quality of the work consequential."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7ff88ae21a792b1c3567", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.3.12", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "contrasting materials laid on foundation", "note": "The commentary's firm fabric and sound bricks imply that materials matter; Paul lists lasting and combustible materials a builder might place on the foundation, preparing for the fire test in the next verse."}
{"connection_id": "BC-dda0145e7ddd160569d9", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.3.13", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "each person’s work is tested by fire", "note": "The commentary links work to a structure that can hold or fail; Paul says fire will disclose and test each builder’s work, adding an explicit test of what construction can endure."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e9f53f4216394986abc5", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.3.13", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "each builder's work tested by fire", "note": "The commentary distinguishes structurally sound deeds from apparent construction; Paul says fire will disclose each builder's work, adding a test of workmanship to the building image."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c3574daead76da7d2059", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.3.15", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "builder suffers loss while escaping", "note": "The commentary's bad foundation carries its builder into loss; Paul says the builder whose work burns suffers loss though the person is saved, a distinct outcome that makes the comparison an uncertain reversal."}
{"connection_id": "BC-fa4c3f3061ee4d3617c2", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.3.9", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "coworkers and God's building", "note": "The commentary turns individual works into a collective building; Paul calls his fellow ministers God's coworkers and the community God's building, identifying both laborers and structure."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2a8156165f448365efc3", "ref": "SBLGNT:1John.3.18", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "love in deed and truth", "note": "The commentary puts work and haqq together in a constructive account; 1 John says love must be shown in deed and truth, pairing action with truth while warning against speech alone."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4ef4f696ec2898d14c99", "ref": "SBLGNT:1John.3.18", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "deed and truth together", "note": "The commentary joins firm truthful speech to constructive works; the letter urges love in deed and truth rather than words alone, making both elements necessary to a real bond."}
{"connection_id": "BC-915f9b0e8f9819fcb5dd", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Pet.2.5", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "living stones built into a spiritual house", "note": "The commentary turns building and joined pieces into a moral image; 1 Peter calls its readers living stones being built into a spiritual house, giving communal construction a religious interpretation."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b18add87d0e435e15628", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Pet.2.5", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "living stones built into a spiritual house", "note": "The commentary makes individual deeds into bricks of a common structure; 1 Peter calls believers living stones being built into a spiritual house for worship."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3c6c61aff21da458a4fc", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Pet.2.6", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "yorum_gelenegi", "basis": "Isaiah’s chosen cornerstone applied to Christ", "note": "The commentary’s firm fit and foundation imagery meets Peter’s citation of Isaiah’s tested cornerstone as Christ, adding a Christian interpretation in which trust in the chosen stone prevents shame."}
{"connection_id": "BC-56c727e530ab95a4ca7b", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Thess.5.11", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "encourage and build one another up", "note": "The commentary says counsel joins parts into a sound structure; Paul tells the community both to encourage one another and to build one another up, transferring the construction image to mutual support."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cc9aa77affde18a27539", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Thess.5.11", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "encourage and build one another", "note": "The commentary turns reciprocal counsel into building; the letter commands believers to encourage and build up one another in the same breath."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ed2ceac35fecf02751d1", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Thess.5.14", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "admonish; help; patience toward all", "note": "The ayah's reciprocal counsel and patience appear together; the letter directs the community to admonish the disorderly, support the weak, and be patient toward all."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b90c1bf03974c619f4f3", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Tim.3.15", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "house as pillar and support of truth", "note": "The commentary joins a stable house to حق as firm truth; 1 Timothy calls God's household the pillar and support of the truth, making the structural image explicit."}
{"connection_id": "BC-12580bd901c07c0116a1", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.13.11", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "restoration and mutual encouragement", "note": "The commentary pairs repairing what is spoiled with counsel that joins people; Paul's closing charge asks the community to pursue restoration, encourage one another, agree, and live in peace."}
{"connection_id": "BC-254b755c9b5fcfa22312", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Thess.3.13", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "do not tire of doing good", "note": "The commentary makes righteous work something held together by patience; the letter directly tells brothers not to grow weary in doing good, identifying fatigue as a threat to the work."}
{"connection_id": "BC-81795ed93cd4fea5d642", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Tim.2.19", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "firm foundation paired with turning from iniquity", "note": "The commentary opposes sound construction to a weak house and corruption; 2 Timothy says God’s firm foundation stands, then pairs its seal with the command to depart from iniquity, joining structural security to ethical conduct."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2eaaaadbeca87221b8f4", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Tim.2.19", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "firm foundation; inscription; turning from wrong", "note": "The commentary puts firmly set truth beside deeds that repair corruption; this verse joins God's firm foundation and its inscribed seal to a call for everyone naming the Lord to turn from unrighteousness."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c2428298f4b41c7371c3", "ref": "SBLGNT:Col.2.19", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "joints and ligaments hold body together", "note": "The source's حق includes the place where bones meet; Colossians says the whole body is supplied and held together by joints and ligaments, making the anatomical join a figure for communal growth."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e153b95980550e2ece06", "ref": "SBLGNT:Col.2.2", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "hearts knit together in love", "note": "The commentary says mutual advice connects pieces and haqq makes the weave firm; Colossians speaks of hearts knit together in love and reaching full assurance, linking cohesion with shared understanding."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b85941d000e4a3967abf", "ref": "SBLGNT:Col.2.2", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "hearts encouraged and knit together in love", "note": "The commentary makes reciprocal counsel join parts into one whole; Paul seeks encouraged hearts joined together in love as they reach assured understanding, giving verbal support and cohesion one purpose."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4f308baa95b2d0f779f0", "ref": "SBLGNT:Col.3.13", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "bear with and forgive one another", "note": "The commentary makes repair a reciprocal act that reconnects parts; Colossians orders believers to bear with and forgive one another when a complaint separates them."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8bb3a7dc0e77a5fe8ae2", "ref": "SBLGNT:Col.3.14", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "love binds virtues into completeness", "note": "The commentary says one piece is attached to another to form a firm whole; Colossians calls love the bond of completeness over the listed virtues, translating that join into moral practice."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3d8fb7cc8fdaadcad884", "ref": "SBLGNT:Col.3.16", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "teaching and admonishing one another", "note": "The commentary says tavsiye joins the pieces of a community through sound words; Colossians has the word of Christ dwell in them as they teach and admonish one another."}
{"connection_id": "BC-81395f7ea7768138f14c", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.2.20", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "foundation and cornerstone", "note": "The source compares sound and collapsing foundations; Ephesians describes the household of God as built on an apostolic and prophetic foundation with Christ as cornerstone."}
{"connection_id": "BC-de567cdd044eb9fa4c1d", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.2.21", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "whole structure joined and growing into a temple", "note": "The commentary fits parts into a secure structure; Ephesians describes the whole building being joined together and growing into a holy temple, an architectural image for a community."}
{"connection_id": "BC-918ea933c11fb667377c", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.2.21", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "whole building fitted together", "note": "The commentary's door fits its place and each piece is joined; Ephesians says the whole building is joined together and grows into a holy temple."}
{"connection_id": "BC-93384221ad70a0636047", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.15", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "truth spoken in love grows the body", "note": "The commentary makes حق firm speech within a joined community; Ephesians couples speaking truth in love with growth into Christ, placing truthful words inside the body's construction."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d1338902d64ef6f16a06", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.16", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "body held together by joints; each part works", "note": "The commentary joins work, repair, and fitted parts in one structure; Ephesians describes a body joined through its joints, with each part working as it should so the whole builds itself up."}

{"connection_id": "BC-d12b6d0ce998bae0510b", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.16", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "joints; each part working; body built up", "note": "The commentary joins the bones' meeting place, attached pieces, and useful work; Ephesians says every joint supplies the body as each part works and the body builds itself up."}
{"connection_id": "BC-280f54ba5d88e88a2280", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.2", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "patience while bearing one another", "note": "The commentary's reciprocal joining must endure strain; Ephesians asks believers to bear with one another in love with humility, gentleness, and patience before urging unity."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8ac5e0c3b58fb40d6048", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.25", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "speak truth to neighbor; members of one another", "note": "The commentary makes mutual counsel connect people; Ephesians tells each person to speak truth with a neighbor because they are members of one another, joining truthful speech to communal interdependence."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d4d170e632cf83a1e4aa", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.25", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "truth spoken because members belong together", "note": "The commentary makes firm truth and attaching parts mutually reinforcing; Ephesians commands truth to one's neighbor on the ground that people are members of one another."}
{"connection_id": "BC-94478ece5d434102c30b", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.29", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "speech good for building others up", "note": "The commentary calls firm speech part of communal construction; Ephesians directs speakers to say what is good for building up hearers according to need."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2ba0070bebde41041967", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.3", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "unity kept in a bond of peace", "note": "The source says recommendation attaches one part to another; Ephesians directs believers to maintain the Spirit's unity in the bond of peace, expressing an ethical joining before its jointed-body image."}
{"connection_id": "BC-93fa84a02593d66124ad", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.1", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "restore a person caught in fault", "note": "The commentary defines صالحات through repair rather than corruption; Galatians directs spiritually minded believers to restore an erring person gently, making repair a communal deed."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a457f6dc5b8c12e9aa47", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.10", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "do good especially to faith's household", "note": "The commentary treats righteous work as building a community; Galatians urges doing good to everyone, especially the household of faith, identifying the circle in which the work strengthens bonds."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0c13728f9838aa2da92a", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.2", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "carry one another's burdens", "note": "The commentary makes reciprocal action prevent a part from failing; Galatians tells believers to bear one another's burdens and thereby fulfill Christ's law."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a6348105c64d2c8a08ae", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.9", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "persist in doing good until harvest", "note": "The ayah joins good deeds with mutual counsel in patience; Galatians tells the community not to tire of doing good because a harvest comes if they do not give up, giving endurance a concrete gain."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8221a2ec70428840c33d", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.10.24", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "stir one another to love and good works", "note": "The commentary’s mutual counsel connects people in constructive action; Hebrews asks readers to consider one another and stir each other toward love and good works, making that reciprocity explicitly ethical."}
{"connection_id": "BC-1ea6c96d6f0f0fe4a52b", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.10.24", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "one another prompted to good deeds", "note": "The ayah's reciprocal exhortation and good deeds are presented as pieces of one structure; Hebrews asks believers to consider one another so as to stir love and good works."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f04fa3b8313dad8faf72", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.10.25", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "encouraging one another", "note": "The source commentary says recommendation attaches persons like pieces; Hebrews enjoins mutual encouragement in the gathered community, specifying the practice that holds it together."}
{"connection_id": "BC-55460b9ee2930c172390", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.10.36", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "endurance after doing God's will", "note": "The ayah names patience alongside good action; Hebrews says believers need endurance so that, having done God's will, they receive the promise, tying perseverance to completed action."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7c7fad05557df204ae1c", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.12.13", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "joint kept from failing and healed", "note": "The source's حق can name where bones meet while صالح means repair; Hebrews calls for straight paths so a lame limb is not put out of joint but healed, joining both anatomical fit and restoration."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0e677dcadc18f6b53ee8", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.3.13", "target": "sec12", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "exhort one another daily against deception", "note": "The commentary makes mutual counsel part of a sound communal structure; Hebrews calls for daily mutual exhortation so no one is hardened by sin’s deceit, showing counsel as protection against moral failure."}
